-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                                  APPLICATION                                  
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

To run the application, activate the "ever2e" executable.

Emulated disk support is not yet implemented, but pre-generated files can be
loaded into the emulator at startup by setting "ever2e.exe" as the default
application used to open ".bas" files and then double clicking on the desired
program.

A few sample programs are included with the application.

License information can be found in the file "LICENSE"

Bugs reports / comments can be submitted here:
http://www.cursorcorner.net/contact.php


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                          CROSS-PLATFORM BUILD (CMAKE)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This repo now uses CMake/CTest as the source of truth for all platforms.

From the repository root:

    cmake --preset macos-release
    cmake --build --preset macos-release
    ctest --preset macos-release

Platform presets:
- macOS: `macos-release`
- Linux: `linux-release`
- Windows: `windows-release`

CI tiers (GitHub Actions):
- Smoke: `./scripts/macos/run_smoke.sh`
- Main tests: `./scripts/macos/run_main_tests.sh`

`ever2e` requires a positional `.emu` path:

    ./build/macos/ever2e release/Apple2eNoSlots.emu --headless --steps 1000


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                               MACOS QUICK START
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

From the repository root:

    ./scripts/macos/build.sh
    ./scripts/macos/run.sh
    ./scripts/macos/run_smoke.sh
    ./scripts/macos/run_trace_baseline.sh
    ./scripts/macos/run_main_tests.sh
    ./scripts/macos/run_microcode_tests.sh
    ./scripts/macos/run_generated_tests.sh

Direct binary usage (required positional `.emu` config):

    ./build/macos/ever2e release/Apple2eNoSlots.emu
    ./build/macos/ever2e release/Apple2eNoSlots.emu --headless --steps 1000
    ./build/macos/ever2e release/Apple2eNoSlots.emu --rom-file /absolute/path/to/APPLE2E.ROM --headless --steps 1000

Recording video/audio:

    ./build/macos/ever2e release/Apple2eNoSlots.emu \
        --headless \
        --paste-file samples/quick_flip.bas \
        --steps 20000000 \
        --record-video build/recordings/quick_flip_headless.mkv

`--record-video` writes a Matroska file with FFV1 video and signed 16-bit mono
PCM audio. Headless recording renders the emulator display to an offscreen
560x384 raster buffer instead of scraping the dummy SDL window, and it waits for
the encoder rather than dropping video frames. Windowed recording uses the same
recorder but may drop frames if encoding falls behind so interactive emulation
stays responsive.

Optional cleanup:

    ./scripts/macos/clean.sh

Notes:
- `build.sh` now builds both `ever2e` and `microcode_tests`.
- `run.sh` and `run_microcode_tests.sh` rebuild by default to avoid stale binaries.
  Set `REBUILD_ON_RUN=0` to skip rebuild.
- The run script starts from "release/" so ROM/assets resolve correctly.
- `run.sh` auto-resolves `.emu` paths from `release/` and defaults to
  `Apple2eNoSlots.emu` if omitted.
- The emulator now requires a positional `.emu` config path (no `--emu` flag).
- A default config is provided at `release/Apple2eNoSlots.emu`.
- ROM loading follows `binary.file` from the `.emu` config (relative paths are
  resolved from the `.emu` file directory).
- `--rom-file` overrides `.emu` `binary.file` for a run.
- Scripts accept `ROM_FILE=/absolute/path/to/APPLE2E.ROM` and pass it through.
- Scripts also support `ROM_GENERATED=loop` to generate a temporary zero-padded
  16KB ROM that loops forever at `$C000` (not committed to repo).
- If SDL is installed in a non-standard location, set PKG_CONFIG_PATH before
  running build.sh.
- `run_smoke.sh` is a quick headless sanity check:
  - default `ROM_GENERATED=loop` (temporary 16KB loop ROM, not committed)
  - default `STEPS=12`
  - default final PC check `REQUIRE_HALT_PC=0xC000`
- `run_trace_baseline.sh` is a short deterministic trace parity check:
  - generates a temporary 16KB loop ROM on the fly (not committed)
  - writes fresh run trace to `build/macos/trace_loop_actual.csv`
  - compares against `tests/baselines/cpp_loop_trace_verbose.csv`
  - to refresh baseline intentionally:
    - `UPDATE_BASELINE=1 ./scripts/macos/run_trace_baseline.sh`
- `run_main_tests.sh` is the primary full test entrypoint:
  - `run_microcode_tests.sh`
  - `run_generated_tests.sh`
- `run_generated_tests.sh` runs the long generated test paste-loader with default
  halt addresses:
  - PASS loop: `0x33D2`
  - FAIL loop: `0x33C0`
  - Runs in unthrottled headless mode for faster bounded runs
  - Uses `release/Apple2eNoSlots.emu` by default (override with `EMU_FILE=...`)
  - Override with env vars if needed:
    - `STEPS=120000000 ./scripts/macos/run_generated_tests.sh`
    - `EMU_FILE=/path/to/config.emu ./scripts/macos/run_generated_tests.sh`
    - `HALT_EXECUTION=0x1234,0x5678 ./scripts/macos/run_generated_tests.sh`
- `run_microcode_tests.sh` and `run_generated_tests.sh` remain available for
   isolating failures.
 - Example custom ROM runs:
   - `ROM_FILE=/absolute/path/to/APPLE2E.ROM ./scripts/macos/run_smoke.sh`
   - `ROM_FILE=/absolute/path/to/APPLE2E.ROM ./scripts/macos/run_main_tests.sh`
   - `ROM_GENERATED=loop ./scripts/macos/run_smoke.sh`
   - `REQUIRE_HALT_PC=0xC000 STEPS=12 ./scripts/macos/run_smoke.sh`


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                                  COMPILATION                                  
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Compilation is multi-platform. Supported platforms are listed on the SDL
website.

Get source code from;
http://cursorcorner.net/project.html

Install SDL and SDL_image developer libraries:
http://www.libsdl.org/
http://www.libsdl.org/projects/SDL_image/

Install FFmpeg developer libraries to enable `--record-video`. If FFmpeg is not
available at configure time, the emulator still builds but recording support is
disabled.

Under Windows '98 or later:
Compile using msysgit or Microsoft Visual C++.
Originally compiled using msysgit and Eclipse C/C++ (project files included)
Git for Windows (msysgit) can be downloaded at http://msysgit.github.com/
link using SDL and SDL_IMAGE libraries

Under Linux:
use g++ to compile all source files in src directory
link using SDL and SDL_IMAGE libraries

Under Mac:
Some of the key names need to be modified in "keytrans2e.cpp" to match Mac
layout.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                                  KNOWN BUGS                                   
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DHIRES bits should start scanning 7 pixels before HIRES bits. Could add an
8-pixel border around a 567x384 screen to make 583x400 windowed mode and
640x480 in full screen mode. This shift would eliminate the need for an
alternate DHIRES palette and more accurately represents the expected IIe
behavior.

The color palette is slightly off. Greys, white, and 3-bit pastel colors should
all have twice the intensity of 1 and 2-bit colors.

If you press escape to exit F1 menu, first character of input is not deleted
for ever2e testinput.txt file. If you press F1, it is. Extra space inserted
for now as temporary solution.

Should put a freeze on keyboard input while automated input is being processed.

The following crashes the program: F1 toggle while executing BASIC program.
This is likely because the CPU state is not yet saved properly.

Add save state

Working directory is lost when ever2e is indirectly called, causing the icon
to disappear and other potential side-effects. This can be fixed by reading
arg[0] and determining working directory (default "./").

Minor - Open and closed apple keys can not be pressed at the same time.

Minor - Initial state of caps-lock key is unknown.

Minor - CPU speed modifies video sync timing applications - should draw
every nth frame n times faster to avoid this problem. Use "test_split.bas"
for an example of the bug (which is actually also a problem with hardware
speed enhancements on the Apple IIe).

Minor - The speaker tick waveform is very closely matched by the emulator, but
to get a more precise static pattern of an Apple IIe may require recording a
single speaker toggle in both directions. The static pattern is surprisingly
stable between toggles. More research has also shown that the toggle air-
pressure should be higher when switching from the relaxed to tense diaphragm
state. The air-pressure physics calculation may be slightly off as well. It is
currently modeled after spring physics.
